---
---

<section id="architecture" class="py-24 relative bg-background/60 border-t border-b border-border">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-16">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3.5 py-1 rounded-full bg-surface border border-secondary/40 text-xs font-mono text-track-annotation mb-4">
        <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 text-track-annotation" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
          <polyline points="4 17 10 11 4 5"/><line x1="12" y1="19" x2="20" y2="19"/>
        </svg>
        UNDER THE HOOD
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground font-['Outfit']">
        Built with Modern Systems Architecture
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base sm:text-lg text-muted-foreground">
        Designed from first principles to isolate native system performance from lightweight web presentation.
      </p>
    </div>

    {/* Architecture Grid */}
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
      {/* Pillar 1: Native Rust Core */}
      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-surface border border-border relative overflow-hidden flex flex-col justify-between">
        <div>
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-primary/15 border border-primary/30 text-track-screen flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <rect x="4" y="4" width="16" height="16" rx="2"/><rect x="9" y="9" width="6" height="6"/><path d="M15 2v2M9 2v2M15 20v2M9 20v2M20 15h2M20 9h2M2 15h2M2 9h2"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <span class="text-xs font-mono text-track-screen uppercase font-semibold">Native Backend</span>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mt-1">Rust + Tauri v2 Core</h3>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-2 leading-relaxed">
            Directly hooks into Windows Graphics Capture (WGC) and Direct3D 11 swapchains. 
            Eliminates multi-process Electron bloat while maintaining sub-millisecond command execution.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-6 p-3 rounded-lg bg-background border border-border text-[11px] font-mono text-muted-foreground space-y-1">
          <div class="text-track-mic font-semibold">&bull; Direct3D 11 Hardware Texture Buffer</div>
          <div>&bull; Multi-threaded Zero-Copy Worker Pool</div>
          <div>&bull; Windows Credential Manager OS Vault</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      {/* Pillar 2: WebAssembly Overlay */}
      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-surface border border-border relative overflow-hidden flex flex-col justify-between">
        <div>
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-secondary/15 border border-secondary/30 text-track-annotation flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <polyline points="16 18 22 12 16 6"/><polyline points="8 6 2 12 8 18"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <span class="text-xs font-mono text-track-annotation uppercase font-semibold">Deterministic Execution</span>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mt-1">WebAssembly Engine</h3>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-2 leading-relaxed">
            The canonical overlay evaluator is compiled directly from Rust to WebAssembly. 
            The React frontend and FFmpeg export engine share the exact same mathematical layout formulas.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-6 p-3 rounded-lg bg-background border border-border text-[11px] font-mono text-muted-foreground space-y-1">
          <div class="text-track-annotation font-semibold">&bull; 100% Export vs Preview Parity</div>
          <div>&bull; Subpixel Bezier Smoothing Calculation</div>
          <div>&bull; Shared contracts via Turborepo monorepo</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      {/* Pillar 3: SQLite Journaling */}
      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-surface border border-border relative overflow-hidden flex flex-col justify-between">
        <div>
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-track-mic/15 border border-track-mic/30 text-track-mic flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <ellipse cx="12" cy="5" rx="9" ry="3"/><path d="M21 12c0 1.66-4 3-9 3s-9-1.34-9-3"/><path d="M3 5v14c0 1.66 4 3 9 3s9-1.34 9-3V5"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <span class="text-xs font-mono text-track-mic uppercase font-semibold">Crash Resilience</span>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mt-1">SQLite Session Journal</h3>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-2 leading-relaxed">
            Every timeline edit, marker, audio segment, and telemetry point is written sequentially via 
            Write-Ahead Logging (WAL). Unfinished sessions are reconstructed seamlessly upon restart.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-6 p-3 rounded-lg bg-background border border-border text-[11px] font-mono text-muted-foreground space-y-1">
          <div class="text-track-mic font-semibold">&bull; ACID Transaction Safety</div>
          <div>&bull; Write-Ahead Log (WAL) Synchronous Mode</div>
          <div>&bull; Zero corrupted video containers</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
